From: Deyan Petrov <25847560+deyanp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 12:10:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] feat: add ESP32-C6 support

Adds an ESP32-C6 compile target, its device documentation, and moves CI onto a
current ESPHome.

Hardware verified: ESP32-C6-DevKitC-1 (ESP32-C6-WROOM-1) with a CC1101 868 MHz
module. The firmware boots, joins WiFi, brings the CC1101 up (MARCSTATE=0x0d,
RX), and receives valid Elero frames with `crc_ok: true` at the default
frequency preset.

- `tests/test.esp32-c6-idf.yaml`, modelled on `test.esp32-mqtt.yaml`. Chip
  select is on GPIO6, not the GPIO5 used by the generic ESP32 wiring: GPIO5 is
  a strapping pin on the C6 (ESPHome's own strapping set for the part is
  {4, 5, 8, 9, 15}). GDO0 is on GPIO3.

- `test.esp32-c6-idf` added to the `esphome-compile` matrix.

- `docs/devices/esp32-c6-cc1101.md` with the C6 pinout, the strapping-pin
  warning, the CC1101 3.3 V-only warning, and the frequency preset table.
  Linked from the README device list.

- CI container moved from `ghcr.io/esphome/esphome:2026.2.2` to `2026.8.1`, and
  the `esphome==` dev pin moved to match. `requires-python` goes to >=3.12
  because ESPHome 2026.8.1 requires it, and `uv.lock` is regenerated. The stale
  pin is why the `logger::LogListener` removal went unnoticed.

